From: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:14:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: s390: pci: Reject adapter interrupt forwarding if
 already enabled
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.44
Git-commit: 8fa01be5a6149404adb82c0979a78f6347edd3ef

commit 8fa01be5a6149404adb82c0979a78f6347edd3ef upstream.

The MPCIFC instruction doesn't allow registering adapter interrupts without
first unregistering. So reject any request to enable interrupt forwarding
if its already enabled for the zPCI device. This also fixes overwriting and
thus leaking resources when the ioctl is called multiple times for the same
device.

Fixes: 3c5a1b6f0a18 ("KVM: s390: pci: provide routines for enabling/disabling interrupt forwarding")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reviewed-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>
Reviewed-by: Matthew Rosato <mjrosato@linux.ibm.com>
Signed-off-by: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Tested-by: Matthew Rosato <mjrosato@linux.ibm.com>
Signed-off-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 arch/s390/kvm/pci.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c b/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
index 20f738fa6556..a406e92530ec 100644
--- a/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
+++ b/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
@@ -238,6 +238,10 @@ static int kvm_s390_pci_aif_enable(struct zpci_dev *zdev, struct zpci_fib *fib,
 	if (zdev->gisa == 0)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/* AIF already enabled for the device */
+	if (zdev->kzdev->fib.fmt0.aibv != 0)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	kvm = zdev->kzdev->kvm;
 	msi_vecs = min_t(unsigned int, fib->fmt0.noi, zdev->max_msi);
 
-- 
2.53.0

